From: BDY-G98 port <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 02:10:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] usb: gadget: use 64 KiB RockUSB transfers

RKDevTool writes raw images in 128-sector commands, or 64 KiB at a time.
The mainline RockUSB 4 KiB endpoint buffer splits every command into 16
separate synchronous block writes.  On RK3588 eMMC this limits a direct
image download to about 1 MiB/s.

Use a 64 KiB endpoint and block buffer so each host command is handled by
one USB request and one block write.  Report progress every 128 MiB because
the normal debug messages are compiled out in release builds.

Signed-off-by: BDY-G98 port <noreply@example.invalid>
---
 arch/arm/include/asm/arch-rockchip/f_rockusb.h | 4 ++--
 drivers/usb/gadget/f_rockusb.c                 | 5 +++++
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/include/asm/arch-rockchip/f_rockusb.h b/arch/arm/include/asm/arch-rockchip/f_rockusb.h
--- a/arch/arm/include/asm/arch-rockchip/f_rockusb.h
+++ b/arch/arm/include/asm/arch-rockchip/f_rockusb.h
@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@
 #define RX_ENDPOINT_MAXIMUM_PACKET_SIZE_1_1  0x0040
 #define TX_ENDPOINT_MAXIMUM_PACKET_SIZE      0x0040
 
-#define EP_BUFFER_SIZE			4096
+#define EP_BUFFER_SIZE			(64 * 1024)
 /*
  * EP_BUFFER_SIZE must always be an integral multiple of maxpacket size
  * (64 or 512 or 1024), else we break on certain controllers like DWC3
@@ -27,7 +27,7 @@
  */
 
 #define RKUSB_BUF_SIZE		EP_BUFFER_SIZE * 2
-#define RKBLOCK_BUF_SIZE		4096
+#define RKBLOCK_BUF_SIZE		EP_BUFFER_SIZE
 
 #define RKUSB_STATUS_IDLE			0
 #define RKUSB_STATUS_CMD			1
diff --git a/drivers/usb/gadget/f_rockusb.c b/drivers/usb/gadget/f_rockusb.c
--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/f_rockusb.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/f_rockusb.c
@@ -517,6 +517,11 @@ static void rx_handler_dl_image(struct usb_ep *ep, struct usb_request *req)
 		return;
 	}
 	f_rkusb->lba += blkcnt;
+	if (!(f_rkusb->lba % (128 * 1024 * 1024 / 512))) {
+		printf("Rockusb wrote %llu MiB\n",
+		       (unsigned long long)f_rkusb->lba *
+		       f_rkusb->desc->blksz / (1024 * 1024));
+	}
 
 	/* Check if transfer is done */
 	if (f_rkusb->dl_bytes >= f_rkusb->dl_size) {
-- 
